1
00:00:04,933 --> 00:00:12,067
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:32,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,133 --> 00:00:35,233
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:41,100
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,467 --> 00:00:43,800
[ENGINE REVVING]

6
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:45,067
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,167 --> 00:00:46,333
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,867 --> 00:00:48,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,300
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,767 --> 00:00:53,567
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,667 --> 00:00:55,433
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,100
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:00,433
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,033 --> 00:01:03,100
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:05,133 --> 00:01:06,267
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:08,767
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,167 --> 00:01:11,800
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:12,867
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:23,767
<i>I'll destroy Team Alpha's
trust in each other.</i>

21
00:01:23,867 --> 00:01:25,433
<i> Our researcher said</i>

22
00:01:25,533 --> 00:01:27,933
<i>you've been asking
for General Jacinto's address.</i>

23
00:01:28,033 --> 00:01:28,967
<i> There's a problem, boss.</i>

24
00:01:29,067 --> 00:01:31,367
<i> The guards won't let us in.</i>

25
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:33,367
<i>- You bastard!
- Let's go!</i>

26
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:35,133
<i>Come on, man!
We might get sued!</i>

27
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:36,433
<i> Secure the gold.</i>

28
00:01:36,533 --> 00:01:38,867
<i>This is just the beginning
of the Zafras' downfall.</i>

29
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,133
<i> NLEA raided our warehouse.</i>

30
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:42,833
<i> You have to steal the gold</i>

31
00:01:42,933 --> 00:01:44,367
<i>before it gets
to the safe house.</i>

32
00:01:44,533 --> 00:01:45,733
<i> We're going to get along.</i>

33
00:01:45,867 --> 00:01:47,167
<i> I'll talk to Gabo.</i>

34
00:01:47,267 --> 00:01:48,200
<i>So if things don't go
according to plan,</i>

35
00:01:48,367 --> 00:01:49,533
<i> he'll have to take the blame.</i>

36
00:01:49,700 --> 00:01:52,000
<i>It's Rudy's birthday.
We'll go there and talk to them.</i>

37
00:01:52,167 --> 00:01:54,000
<i>Whenever we have time
to have some fun,</i>

38
00:01:54,167 --> 00:01:55,900
<i>- we make the most of it.
- Mm-hmm.</i>

39
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:58,000
<i> They live differently here.</i>

40
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,500
<i>Back at home,
when there's an occasion,</i>

41
00:01:59,667 --> 00:02:01,500
<i>we get stressed out
just from planning it.</i>

42
00:02:01,667 --> 00:02:04,500
<i>But here, it's enough that
they can get together.</i>

43
00:02:05,567 --> 00:02:07,700
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

44
00:02:09,033 --> 00:02:10,067
I'm warning you, Borromeo!

45
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:12,033
Don't mess with my game plan!

46
00:02:12,333 --> 00:02:13,700
Why are you so mad?

47
00:02:14,300 --> 00:02:15,400
I was helping you!

48
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:16,933
You suck at this whole thing,
you know?

49
00:02:17,067 --> 00:02:18,200
[MAN 1] They're arguing!

50
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:19,900
We'll get exposed
if you keep messing up!

51
00:02:20,267 --> 00:02:21,767
- Such a show-off!
- Oh, yeah?

52
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:23,033
- Try me!
- Hey!

53
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:25,433
- You're gonna blow our cover!
- So you think you're tough?

54
00:02:25,567 --> 00:02:27,400
- That's enough!
- Come on, prove it!

55
00:02:27,567 --> 00:02:29,700
- Let's do this!
- No, no! Stop!

56
00:02:29,867 --> 00:02:30,833
[MAN 2] Show him!

57
00:02:30,933 --> 00:02:32,233
Don't mess with me!

58
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,433
[MAN 3] Punch him!

59
00:02:33,567 --> 00:02:35,167
What, you think
I'm scared of you?

60
00:02:35,267 --> 00:02:36,767
- Hey, stop this!
- You bastard!

61
00:02:37,467 --> 00:02:38,867
- Cut it out!
- [KAREN] Excuse me!

62
00:02:39,033 --> 00:02:40,233
Hey! Borromeo!

63
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:41,867
That's enough! Enough!

64
00:02:41,967 --> 00:02:43,567
[MAN 4] Let them fight!

65
00:02:43,733 --> 00:02:44,700
[CASTOR] What the heck?

66
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,900
Stop this!

67
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,700
Karen, call the boss!

68
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:48,800
He's on the line.

69
00:02:49,267 --> 00:02:50,767
Hello? Where are you?

70
00:02:50,933 --> 00:02:52,367
These two are brawling
on the basketball court!

71
00:02:52,467 --> 00:02:53,700
Stop provoking each other!

72
00:02:53,800 --> 00:02:55,733
- Come on! Fight me!
- Hey! I said, enough!

73
00:02:56,767 --> 00:02:58,233
Come on! Let's do this!

74
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,967
- [KAREN] Stop it, Borromeo!
- [CASTOR] Cut it out already!

75
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:01,233
Get it together, you two!

76
00:03:01,767 --> 00:03:02,767
Stop it!

77
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:04,767
[CASTOR] Hey! Enough fighting!

78
00:03:04,933 --> 00:03:06,267
- Let it go!
- Calm down!

79
00:03:06,433 --> 00:03:07,767
- He just won't stop.
- Hey!

80
00:03:08,567 --> 00:03:09,867
[SEBASTIAN] What's happening?

81
00:03:09,967 --> 00:03:11,400
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

82
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:14,767
These two keep going
at each other's throats!

83
00:03:15,967 --> 00:03:17,400
What's going on with you two?

84
00:03:17,833 --> 00:03:19,067
You're acting like fools!

85
00:03:19,167 --> 00:03:22,067
[CROWD MURMURING]

86
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:24,767
Get out, you outsiders!

87
00:03:24,867 --> 00:03:26,067
This isn't your town!

88
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:27,567
Go on, leave now!

89
00:03:27,667 --> 00:03:28,967
[CROWD CLAMORING]

90
00:03:29,133 --> 00:03:30,300
We're so sorry.
Let's go!

91
00:03:30,467 --> 00:03:32,167
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING]

92
00:03:32,300 --> 00:03:33,767
- Don't ever come back!
- Come on!

93
00:03:33,867 --> 00:03:35,167
[KAREN] Stop it!

94
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:36,767
Never return here!

95
00:03:37,867 --> 00:03:39,767
These outsiders...

96
00:03:39,867 --> 00:03:41,767
[GLOOMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

97
00:03:41,933 --> 00:03:43,267
Always causing trouble!

98
00:03:43,367 --> 00:03:45,267
[INDISTINCT CROWD CHATTER]

99
00:03:45,433 --> 00:03:47,333
A bunch of troublemakers.
They're not even locals!

100
00:03:47,467 --> 00:03:48,800
[MAN 5] Stupid outsiders...

101
00:03:48,967 --> 00:03:50,267
- [MAN 6] Come on, dude.
- Yeah.

102
00:03:50,433 --> 00:03:52,267
- What a waste of time.
- You can say that again.

103
00:03:52,433 --> 00:03:54,600
Let's go home, man.
Damn cowards!

104
00:03:54,733 --> 00:03:55,633
[MUSIC ENDS]

105
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:57,633
Sir.

106
00:03:57,733 --> 00:04:01,967
Fifty kilos of gold bars
worth 400 million pesos.

107
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:05,167
We also recovered loose jewelry,

108
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:07,800
along with a ledger
containing transactions

109
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:10,500
dating back one year.

110
00:04:10,967 --> 00:04:12,333
Phew!

111
00:04:12,867 --> 00:04:15,267
Separate the gold bars
from the rest of the evidence.

112
00:04:15,367 --> 00:04:17,800
Nobody touches anything
without my clearance.

113
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:19,933
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

114
00:04:20,033 --> 00:04:21,300
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

115
00:04:21,467 --> 00:04:24,033
[PHONE RINGING]

116
00:04:24,167 --> 00:04:25,500
I'll just take this call.

117
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:31,033
[RICARDO] Domingo,

118
00:04:31,200 --> 00:04:32,333
<i>transfer the gold
from your precinct</i>

119
00:04:32,433 --> 00:04:34,700
to the NLEA safe house.

120
00:04:34,867 --> 00:04:36,500
Sir, that's going to be
a long process.

121
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:38,700
The gold is safe
at our precinct.

122
00:04:38,867 --> 00:04:41,167
You seem to foget
I'm a former NLEA.

123
00:04:41,567 --> 00:04:42,833
<i> I know the people there,</i>

124
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,167
<i> from then until now.</i>

125
00:04:44,333 --> 00:04:47,667
You do realize how much a single
gold bar is worth today, right?

126
00:04:48,567 --> 00:04:50,867
Yes, sir. More or less.

127
00:04:51,567 --> 00:04:52,867
- [DOMINGO MUMBLES]
- [SANTOS WHISPERS] Melchor...

128
00:04:53,033 --> 00:04:54,467
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

129
00:04:54,567 --> 00:04:56,167
This is a lot of money.

130
00:04:56,700 --> 00:04:58,667
How much is one gold bar now?

131
00:04:59,267 --> 00:05:00,200
This one?

132
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,600
Eight million pesos each.

133
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,033
- Wow, that really is expensive.
- [SCOFFS]

134
00:05:05,467 --> 00:05:08,367
Do you think
they'll notice what we took?

135
00:05:08,533 --> 00:05:10,200
That's just loose change
for them.

136
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:11,867
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

137
00:05:11,967 --> 00:05:12,933
[SANTOS EXHALES]

138
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,733
[SLAPS]

139
00:05:15,867 --> 00:05:17,500
[WHISPERS]
There's tons of these!

140
00:05:19,100 --> 00:05:22,433
[RICARDO] If you put someone
in that kind of situation,

141
00:05:23,567 --> 00:05:25,033
they'll surely be tempted.

142
00:05:25,133 --> 00:05:26,533
So move the gold now.

143
00:05:26,700 --> 00:05:28,200
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

144
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:29,767
Yes... sir.

145
00:05:31,933 --> 00:05:32,900
[THUDS]

146
00:05:42,233 --> 00:05:43,300
[GLASS THUDS]

147
00:05:45,067 --> 00:05:46,067
[ISOBEL] Thank you, Twinkle.

148
00:05:46,967 --> 00:05:48,867
- Please bring the honey.
- Oh, yes, ma'am.

149
00:05:48,967 --> 00:05:49,967
It's right here.

150
00:05:51,433 --> 00:05:52,200
[CUTLERY CLINKS IN DISTANCE]

151
00:05:52,300 --> 00:05:53,267
Ma'am?

152
00:05:53,433 --> 00:05:54,900
- Yes?
- Ma'am Pinky is here.

153
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,233
Isobel...

154
00:05:56,400 --> 00:05:58,233
Oh, my dear Pinky...

155
00:05:58,333 --> 00:06:00,733
Isobel, do we have
any updates on Sam?

156
00:06:02,933 --> 00:06:04,600
Honestly, up to now
there's still nothing.

157
00:06:04,767 --> 00:06:07,933
But this morning, some people
from NLEA came here.

158
00:06:08,667 --> 00:06:10,067
What for?

159
00:06:10,167 --> 00:06:11,433
To bring bad news?

160
00:06:11,533 --> 00:06:14,267
I only know pieces
of the puzzle.

161
00:06:14,367 --> 00:06:17,300
And that's all Ricardo wants me
to know.

162
00:06:17,467 --> 00:06:18,633
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

163
00:06:18,800 --> 00:06:22,100
To tell you honestly,
I'm starting to get frustrated!

164
00:06:22,467 --> 00:06:25,500
Maybe Ricardo's doing this

165
00:06:25,633 --> 00:06:29,267
so you won't be
too worried, Isobel.

166
00:06:29,367 --> 00:06:33,300
If I only have a way
to see the big picture,

167
00:06:33,467 --> 00:06:35,100
to know everything.

168
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,100
[BREATH QUIVERING]

169
00:06:36,833 --> 00:06:38,733
I'm so lost.

170
00:06:39,600 --> 00:06:41,967
I don't know what else to do.

171
00:06:42,167 --> 00:06:43,867
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

172
00:06:46,067 --> 00:06:46,967
[ALL CHANTING] Gabo!

173
00:06:47,133 --> 00:06:49,333
Gabo! Gabo! Gabo!

174
00:06:49,500 --> 00:06:50,333
Good evening!

175
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:53,167
[CHEERING, CLAPPING]

176
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:54,800
Pa, this is for you!

177
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:56,700
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

178
00:06:56,833 --> 00:06:58,867
Also, I dedicate this
to my wife.

179
00:06:59,833 --> 00:07:00,800
For Gloria.

180
00:07:02,167 --> 00:07:03,133
I love you!

181
00:07:04,133 --> 00:07:05,433
[TOLITS] For Gloria!

182
00:07:05,533 --> 00:07:11,300
[OVERLAPPING SHOUTING,
CLAPPING]

183
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:14,100
[GABO SINGING]
<i> Now that you're with me</i>

184
00:07:14,533 --> 00:07:16,967
<i> I'm happy</i>

185
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:22,533
<i> No matter what they say</i>

186
00:07:23,367 --> 00:07:29,167
My feelings for you won't change

187
00:07:29,433 --> 00:07:32,300
<i> Day and night</i>

188
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:34,733
<i> You're by my side</i>

189
00:07:36,167 --> 00:07:41,467
<i> I don't need anyone else</i>

190
00:07:42,233 --> 00:07:47,500
<i> My heart is complete</i>

191
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:51,067
[SQUEALING, CLAPPING]

192
00:07:51,233 --> 00:07:57,033
<i> I'll love you</i>

193
00:07:57,133 --> 00:07:59,400
<i> Forever and ever</i>

194
00:08:00,200 --> 00:08:02,700
<i> You're the only one</i>

195
00:08:03,133 --> 00:08:08,733
<i> I want to be with</i>

196
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:14,200
<i> In this life of mine</i>

197
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:17,400
<i> I won't grow weary</i>

198
00:08:17,567 --> 00:08:22,533
<i> Even when we're gray and old</i>

199
00:08:22,667 --> 00:08:26,800
[CHEERING, APPLAUSE]

200
00:08:26,933 --> 00:08:33,900
[LOUD CHEERING,
MUSIC PLAYING IN DISTANCE]

201
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:49,433
<i> I'll love you</i>

202
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:52,200
<i> Forever and ever</i>

203
00:08:53,067 --> 00:08:55,067
<i> You're the only one</i>

204
00:08:55,200 --> 00:09:01,000
<i> I want to be with</i>

205
00:09:01,833 --> 00:09:06,967
<i> In this life of mine</i>

206
00:09:07,133 --> 00:09:08,300
<i> I won't grow weary</i>

207
00:09:08,467 --> 00:09:09,767
[SAM] Scumbag!

208
00:09:10,367 --> 00:09:16,233
<i> Even when we're gray and old</i>

209
00:09:16,333 --> 00:09:17,600
- [CRASHING]
- [SCREAMING]

210
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:18,933
[OBJECTS CLATTER]

211
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,100
[GABO SINGING]
<i> I won't grow weary</i>

212
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:29,100
<i> Even when we're gray and old</i>

213
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:36,000
<i> I won't grow weary of you</i>

214
00:09:36,167 --> 00:09:42,033
<i> For all my life</i>

215
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:43,367
I love you.

216
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:46,967
[SQUEALING, CLAPPING]

217
00:09:47,067 --> 00:09:54,000
["HABANGBUHAY"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

218
00:09:57,400 --> 00:10:00,733
Borromeo, you're lucky
someone stopped us.

219
00:10:00,733 --> 00:10:02,867
Don't worry, Reyes,
this isn't over.

220
00:10:02,900 --> 00:10:04,833
Cut it out, you two!

221
00:10:04,833 --> 00:10:07,767
Bullet has had enough
of you both already.

222
00:10:07,767 --> 00:10:10,767
Don't wait for me
to lose my patience, too.

223
00:10:10,767 --> 00:10:11,933
Ignore them, Karen.

224
00:10:11,933 --> 00:10:14,100
Call Sir Seb so we can go home.

225
00:10:14,100 --> 00:10:15,933
He's the only one
we're waiting for.

226
00:10:15,933 --> 00:10:17,833
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

227
00:10:17,833 --> 00:10:19,633
[ENGINE REVVING]

228
00:10:20,767 --> 00:10:24,067
[PHONE RINGING]

229
00:10:26,767 --> 00:10:30,033
[RINGING CONTINUES]

230
00:10:30,033 --> 00:10:31,667
You're on your own.

231
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:33,900
[LINE RINGING]

232
00:10:33,900 --> 00:10:35,733
He's not picking up.

233
00:10:35,767 --> 00:10:38,267
- I bet he's pissed off.
- [LINE RINGING]

234
00:10:38,267 --> 00:10:41,767
We should head home.
Let's call it a night.

235
00:10:41,767 --> 00:10:43,933
- Come on!
- [ENGINE STARTS]

236
00:10:43,933 --> 00:10:50,900
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

237
00:10:52,133 --> 00:10:53,133
Boss.

238
00:10:53,133 --> 00:10:54,900
- Boss.
- Oh, Salvador.

239
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:56,067
Negative.

240
00:10:58,733 --> 00:11:01,967
We weren't able to
speak to General Jacinto.

241
00:11:01,967 --> 00:11:03,567
That's okay.

242
00:11:03,567 --> 00:11:06,100
We'll make our own story.

243
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:08,100
Dude, it's a miracle.

244
00:11:08,133 --> 00:11:09,833
He's not mad.

245
00:11:09,833 --> 00:11:13,000
We don't need to
interview General Jacinto

246
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,733
to get good ratings.

247
00:11:14,733 --> 00:11:16,733
As long as you go
after him hard,

248
00:11:16,733 --> 00:11:18,900
people will love it.

249
00:11:19,733 --> 00:11:21,767
Are you telling me
to report on a story

250
00:11:21,767 --> 00:11:23,967
I don't know
the whole truth about?

251
00:11:23,967 --> 00:11:25,567
No, no, dude.

252
00:11:25,567 --> 00:11:26,733
The boss is right.

253
00:11:26,733 --> 00:11:29,833
If we entertain the viewers,
our ratings will go up,

254
00:11:29,833 --> 00:11:31,000
the show will make money,

255
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,933
and our pockets will be full.

256
00:11:33,933 --> 00:11:35,833
Jackpot!

257
00:11:35,833 --> 00:11:37,667
- We strike again!
- We strike again!

258
00:11:37,667 --> 00:11:39,167
Goddammit!

259
00:11:39,167 --> 00:11:41,100
How dare they not wake me up?

260
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:44,333
Y'all are going to
regret doing this to me!

261
00:11:44,367 --> 00:11:47,200
What did you think?
That I didn't matter here?

262
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,700
I'm a painting?!

263
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:50,033
Just some decor?!

264
00:11:50,033 --> 00:11:52,267
I can't get this
damn earring in!

265
00:11:52,267 --> 00:11:54,867
[DISTANT CHEERING]

266
00:11:54,867 --> 00:11:57,133
Happy birthday, Pa!

267
00:11:57,133 --> 00:11:59,300
- Thank you, Gabo!
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

268
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:01,267
Cheers!

269
00:12:01,267 --> 00:12:03,100
[APPLAUSE, CHEERING]

270
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:05,833
- [BOTTLES CLINK]
- Bottoms up!

271
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:08,200
Hey!

272
00:12:08,200 --> 00:12:10,267
What is going on here?!

273
00:12:10,267 --> 00:12:12,000
Hmm?!

274
00:12:13,033 --> 00:12:14,800
Seriously?

275
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:19,633
Y'all are shouting
like a bunch of hooligans!

276
00:12:19,633 --> 00:12:21,967
Why the hell
are you so loud?!

277
00:12:21,967 --> 00:12:24,300
Jeez! You're so noisy!

278
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:26,900
Because it's Rudy's birthday!

279
00:12:26,900 --> 00:12:28,700
I know!

280
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:33,867
And no one even bothered
to wake me up

281
00:12:33,867 --> 00:12:37,633
to be here for
Rudy's birthday?!

282
00:12:39,167 --> 00:12:40,667
Huh?

283
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:44,400
Why'd you stop singing?
Keep going!

284
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:46,667
Go ahead! Don't be shy!

285
00:12:46,667 --> 00:12:48,200
Crank it up!

286
00:12:48,233 --> 00:12:51,333
How could they?

287
00:12:51,333 --> 00:12:53,433
The party pooper has arrived.

288
00:12:53,433 --> 00:12:57,400
Excuse me?
I heard that.

289
00:12:57,400 --> 00:13:03,067
Just because I wasn't able to
contribute to this celebration,

290
00:13:03,067 --> 00:13:05,033
I'm the party pooper?

291
00:13:05,033 --> 00:13:07,233
- Now, I'm the bad guy?!
- [BANGS TABLE]

292
00:13:08,933 --> 00:13:10,367
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

293
00:13:10,367 --> 00:13:11,733
[SCOFFS]

294
00:13:11,733 --> 00:13:13,233
So, you're a drunk, too.

295
00:13:14,267 --> 00:13:17,100
I thought you were
a decent woman.

296
00:13:17,100 --> 00:13:20,367
- Where's the food?
- Ignore that woman.

297
00:13:20,367 --> 00:13:22,100
There isn't any more food?!

298
00:13:22,133 --> 00:13:24,767
You didn't save me any food?!

299
00:13:24,767 --> 00:13:27,400
Here.
Just have this.

300
00:13:28,433 --> 00:13:30,800
[BETCHAY] Oh my goodness!

301
00:13:30,800 --> 00:13:32,933
I don't understand

302
00:13:32,933 --> 00:13:35,967
why I'm putting up
with you people!

303
00:13:35,967 --> 00:13:38,833
At least I have a future
working at the bar!

304
00:13:39,700 --> 00:13:42,233
Boy, do I regret getting
involved with you people!

305
00:13:42,233 --> 00:13:46,133
Betchay, do you not
hear yourself?

306
00:13:46,133 --> 00:13:47,433
Hmm?

307
00:13:47,433 --> 00:13:51,800
We were having a blast
before you came!

308
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,100
Oh, sorry!

309
00:13:53,933 --> 00:13:55,333
I'm sorry!

310
00:13:57,767 --> 00:13:59,900
Sorry for spoiling your fun.

311
00:13:59,900 --> 00:14:04,333
I guess I shouldn't have
gotten up.

312
00:14:04,333 --> 00:14:05,700
Sorry!

313
00:14:06,467 --> 00:14:09,267
[SCOFFS] Sorry!

314
00:14:09,267 --> 00:14:12,967
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

315
00:14:12,967 --> 00:14:16,500
[TOTO] Sir, wait a minute.
I need to tell Sir Ricardo...

316
00:14:16,500 --> 00:14:19,233
- Sir! Sir Sebastian is here.
- Hi, sir.

317
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,467
You're back?

318
00:14:20,467 --> 00:14:22,967
Yes, sir.
I just wanted to say hello.

319
00:14:22,967 --> 00:14:25,933
Okay.
Hello. Goodbye.

320
00:14:25,933 --> 00:14:28,067
- It's not a good time.
- But, sir...

321
00:14:28,100 --> 00:14:29,933
- It's not a good time.
- I brought cake. But sir--

322
00:14:29,933 --> 00:14:31,833
It's not a good time.
Thank you.

323
00:14:32,433 --> 00:14:33,967
Ricardo?

324
00:14:35,933 --> 00:14:37,100
Was that Sebastian?

325
00:14:37,100 --> 00:14:38,167
Um...

326
00:14:38,167 --> 00:14:40,433
Toto, open the door.

327
00:14:42,367 --> 00:14:44,000
I heard Miss Isobel.

328
00:14:45,033 --> 00:14:47,867
- Auntie!
- Oh! Any good news?

329
00:14:47,867 --> 00:14:49,867
Sort of good news, Auntie.

330
00:14:49,867 --> 00:14:51,367
And this cake.

331
00:14:51,367 --> 00:14:53,367
[ISOBEL CHUCKLES]

332
00:14:53,367 --> 00:15:00,033
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:15:00,033 --> 00:15:01,800
Auntie, allow me.

334
00:15:01,833 --> 00:15:04,400
[ISOBEL]
Oh, just half a slice for me.

335
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:06,900
I need to watch my sugar intake.

336
00:15:06,900 --> 00:15:13,400
Don't worry about
sugar and calories.

337
00:15:13,400 --> 00:15:16,367
In case no one has told you,

338
00:15:16,367 --> 00:15:20,333
you are both beautiful
and sexy.

339
00:15:20,333 --> 00:15:22,200
- [TWINKLE GUSHES]
- [ISOBEL] Anyway,

340
00:15:22,200 --> 00:15:26,200
Sebastian,
what's the good news?

341
00:15:26,200 --> 00:15:29,367
As you know,
I'm close to finding Sam.

342
00:15:29,367 --> 00:15:31,267
- Yes?
- And when that happens,

343
00:15:32,400 --> 00:15:37,167
I can finally ask
for her hand in marriage.

344
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:39,400
- [ISOBEL CHUCKLES]
- [PINKY] Already?

345
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:41,067
Are you and Sam even together?

346
00:15:41,067 --> 00:15:42,267
Almost.

347
00:15:42,267 --> 00:15:44,233
She's almost my girlfriend.

348
00:15:44,233 --> 00:15:47,200
- Ooh...
- Auntie, honestly...

349
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:49,567
We were going to
make things official.

350
00:15:49,567 --> 00:15:52,233
- [PINKY] Mm-hmm?
- But...

351
00:15:52,233 --> 00:15:55,167
She disappeared that night
she was supposed to say yes.

352
00:15:56,100 --> 00:16:03,067
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

353
00:16:07,100 --> 00:16:10,000
[MAN 1] Gabo! Gabo! Gabo!

354
00:16:10,033 --> 00:16:12,300
- [GUESTS GASP, MURMUR]
- Django's here!

355
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:15,233
- Huh?
- What?!

356
00:16:15,233 --> 00:16:16,867
- [GUNS COCK]
- [MAMENG] Hey! Hey!

357
00:16:16,867 --> 00:16:19,400
Drop your weapons!

358
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:20,633
Come on, Gabo!

359
00:16:20,633 --> 00:16:25,067
[TOLITS] We need to be prepared,
Miss Mameng.

360
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:28,133
- [MAN 2] Yeah!
- [BETHCAY] Hey! Calm down!

361
00:16:28,133 --> 00:16:29,300
Y'all are so paranoid!

362
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:32,300
Are you planning
to kill Django?

363
00:16:32,300 --> 00:16:33,933
Better safe than sorry.

364
00:16:33,933 --> 00:16:34,967
[BETCHAY SCOFFS]

365
00:16:34,967 --> 00:16:39,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

366
00:16:39,433 --> 00:16:42,133
Gabo, who's Django?

367
00:16:42,167 --> 00:16:45,300
He's the reason
I went to jail for eight years.

368
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:48,967
He's my mortal enemy.

369
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:51,567
Stand down.

370
00:16:51,567 --> 00:16:58,567
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

371
00:17:14,400 --> 00:17:18,467
You know, I'm very optimistic
that I'll find Sam.

372
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:19,933
- Okay.
- Mm-hmm.

373
00:17:19,933 --> 00:17:22,067
And I'm optimistic
towards our future.

374
00:17:23,600 --> 00:17:25,500
If it were up to me...

375
00:17:26,367 --> 00:17:28,667
I'd take her out of the NCIA.

376
00:17:28,667 --> 00:17:29,933
- Really?
- Because--

377
00:17:29,933 --> 00:17:33,833
Because I don't like her to be
put in danger. Never, ever!

378
00:17:34,133 --> 00:17:37,300
You mean to say
you'll make her transfer jobs?

379
00:17:37,300 --> 00:17:38,967
- Mm-hmm.
- Into one that's safer?

380
00:17:39,933 --> 00:17:40,967
Oh!

381
00:17:40,967 --> 00:17:44,333
Sebastian, I very much like
what I'm hearing.

382
00:17:44,333 --> 00:17:46,433
Would you please encourage her

383
00:17:46,433 --> 00:17:50,000
to resign from the NCIA
once she returns?

384
00:17:50,033 --> 00:17:52,567
And tell her to find
a different job!

385
00:17:52,567 --> 00:17:55,133
Oh, yes, Auntie.
I will definitely do that.

386
00:17:55,133 --> 00:17:56,333
Yes.

387
00:17:56,333 --> 00:17:58,967
- But I have other plans.
- What?

388
00:18:00,733 --> 00:18:04,300
I won't let her work at all!

389
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:06,467
- Huh?
- I'll make her a princess!

390
00:18:06,467 --> 00:18:08,333
Just so you know...

391
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,267
- I have deep pockets.
- Ahh.

392
00:18:13,700 --> 00:18:16,000
I'm not bragging, but I'm sure.

393
00:18:16,667 --> 00:18:20,333
I'm going to be able
to give Sam a comfortable life.

394
00:18:20,333 --> 00:18:24,733
With Sam's beauty,
she has a lot of admirers.

395
00:18:24,767 --> 00:18:29,167
How sure are you, Seb,
that she'll choose you?

396
00:18:29,167 --> 00:18:33,000
Auntie, who are these guys
you claim can match my level?

397
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,400
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

398
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:39,267
Do they measure up to my looks?

399
00:18:39,267 --> 00:18:40,400
[ISOBEL CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

400
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:44,600
Are they as rich
and smart as me?

401
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:46,533
- [PINKY] Hmm!
- Do these guys come

402
00:18:46,533 --> 00:18:49,067
from a sensible family?

403
00:18:49,067 --> 00:18:53,100
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

404
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:54,200
Auntie.

405
00:18:55,200 --> 00:18:58,167
Who is here now
worrying about Sam?

406
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:03,000
Who's with her now?
Not physically.

407
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:05,000
But soulfully.

408
00:19:06,133 --> 00:19:08,700
- Isn't it me?
- Oh, yeah.

409
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:11,633
- Sebastian Tuazon.
- Hmm...

410
00:19:11,633 --> 00:19:15,700
Samantha Jacinto-Tuazon.

411
00:19:16,467 --> 00:19:19,267
Hm! It rings beautifully.

412
00:19:20,533 --> 00:19:22,367
[SEBASTIAN]
And, Auntie, I'll give Sam

413
00:19:22,367 --> 00:19:25,533
a very beautiful
engagement ring

414
00:19:25,533 --> 00:19:27,233
- [PINKY GASPS]
- and wedding ring.

415
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:31,033
- Auntie, if you'll let me.
- We'll get there.

416
00:19:31,067 --> 00:19:35,733
[ISOBEL CHUCKLES, SIGHS]

417
00:19:37,767 --> 00:19:38,833
Django!

418
00:19:38,833 --> 00:19:41,500
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

419
00:19:41,500 --> 00:19:43,400
What are you doing here
in Paradise?

420
00:19:45,467 --> 00:19:46,467
[PAQUITO] Gabo...

421
00:19:47,167 --> 00:19:50,500
We're not here to cause trouble!

422
00:19:50,500 --> 00:19:56,567
We're here to join the fun
at Rudy's birthday!

423
00:19:56,567 --> 00:19:59,500
- Happy birthday, Rudy!
- [DJANGO CHUCKLES]

424
00:19:59,500 --> 00:20:03,067
[DJANGO] It's true, Gabo.
I'm here to make it up to you.

425
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:06,500
We even brought booze
and food! See?

426
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:09,167
- [DJANGO CHUCKLES]
- [PAQUITO] Give it to them.

427
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:10,800
I don't trust you.

428
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:13,433
You wouldn't come here
for nothing.

429
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,200
What do you want from me?

430
00:20:16,200 --> 00:20:19,333
Hey, Gabo. What's with you?

431
00:20:19,333 --> 00:20:21,767
They're being nice here!

432
00:20:21,767 --> 00:20:26,200
They went here to celebrate
your father's birthday,

433
00:20:26,200 --> 00:20:28,300
and this is how you behave?

434
00:20:28,800 --> 00:20:29,767
Betchay!

435
00:20:31,133 --> 00:20:33,667
I don't need what they have!

436
00:20:33,667 --> 00:20:35,700
[NEIGHBOR] That's right!
Get out of here!

437
00:20:35,733 --> 00:20:42,700
[PEOPLE CLAMORING]

438
00:20:46,633 --> 00:20:48,233
Calm down!

439
00:20:48,233 --> 00:20:50,733
- [NEIGHBOR] Get out of here!
- [PAQUITO] Calm down!

440
00:20:50,733 --> 00:20:54,867
Rudy, we're here to celebrate
your birthday!

441
00:20:54,867 --> 00:20:59,200
We even brought imported beer!
This is expensive!

442
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:02,533
[DJANGO] Give it to them, go!
Hurry up!

443
00:21:02,533 --> 00:21:03,600
Gabo.

444
00:21:04,400 --> 00:21:06,833
Forget about
what happened before.

445
00:21:07,633 --> 00:21:09,733
We're here to have fun.

446
00:21:09,767 --> 00:21:12,167
Don't act like we don't have
good memories together.

447
00:21:12,167 --> 00:21:12,900
We don't!

448
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:15,667
Because you betrayed me!

449
00:21:15,667 --> 00:21:18,200
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

450
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,367
That's why...

451
00:21:20,767 --> 00:21:23,333
I will never believe
anything you say.

452
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:24,633
[BETCHAY] That's enough!

453
00:21:26,333 --> 00:21:29,867
Stop it. That's my boss.

454
00:21:29,867 --> 00:21:33,433
They even brought food
for your father's birthday.

455
00:21:33,433 --> 00:21:35,733
Why are you acting
so aggressively?

456
00:21:38,600 --> 00:21:39,533
[IPE] Gabo.

457
00:21:40,267 --> 00:21:41,333
What's the plan?

458
00:21:42,367 --> 00:21:43,733
I don't trust those guys.

459
00:21:44,533 --> 00:21:46,267
If they make one wrong move...

460
00:21:47,367 --> 00:21:48,467
get them.

461
00:21:48,467 --> 00:21:52,933
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

462
00:21:52,933 --> 00:21:56,767
Fine. If you want
to talk to me, then sit down.

463
00:21:58,267 --> 00:21:59,467
- Let's talk.
- [BETCHAY] Finally.

464
00:21:59,467 --> 00:22:00,767
[BETCHAY CLAPPING]

465
00:22:00,967 --> 00:22:02,767
- Hey, they're visitors.
- [PAQUITO] Thank you, Gabo.

466
00:22:02,767 --> 00:22:03,733
[BETCHAY] Move!

467
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,933
You've got visitors!

468
00:22:07,933 --> 00:22:12,267
Stop sitting, you have visitors!
Actual visitors!

469
00:22:12,267 --> 00:22:18,433
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

470
00:22:19,567 --> 00:22:21,067
Rudy!

471
00:22:21,067 --> 00:22:25,733
I'm sorry we gatecrashed
your birthday party.

472
00:22:25,733 --> 00:22:27,933
[BETCHAY] Oh, boss,
don't worry about it!

473
00:22:27,933 --> 00:22:30,000
You're very welcome here.

474
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,967
And thank you so much
for bringing food.

475
00:22:31,967 --> 00:22:33,567
We finished everything.

476
00:22:33,567 --> 00:22:35,333
And you brought
an expensive bottle of alcohol.

477
00:22:35,333 --> 00:22:36,333
Thank you.

478
00:22:36,333 --> 00:22:37,700
[BETCHAY, PAQUITO CHUCKLE]

479
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:39,900
Django.

480
00:22:41,467 --> 00:22:42,733
What do you want from me?

481
00:22:42,733 --> 00:22:48,633
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

482
00:22:48,667 --> 00:22:50,767
Gabo, we're actually here

483
00:22:51,867 --> 00:22:53,400
to invite you.

484
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,767
We have a big transaction.

485
00:22:56,767 --> 00:23:03,900
[OMINOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

486
00:23:06,967 --> 00:23:08,433
Okay.

487
00:23:08,433 --> 00:23:09,633
Put those away.

488
00:23:09,633 --> 00:23:10,767
Secure the gold bars.

489
00:23:10,767 --> 00:23:12,867
It will be transferred
to the safe house tonight.

490
00:23:12,867 --> 00:23:15,800
But, sir, it's late.
We need to go home.

491
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:17,633
It's General Jacinto's order.

492
00:23:17,633 --> 00:23:19,667
He said the gold
isn't safe here.

493
00:23:19,667 --> 00:23:22,667
Sir, isn't it more dangerous
to move it now?

494
00:23:22,700 --> 00:23:25,533
No one else
knows about this but us.

495
00:23:25,533 --> 00:23:27,633
Besides, General Jacinto
has a point.

496
00:23:28,333 --> 00:23:30,333
Sir, what exactly did he say?

497
00:23:30,333 --> 00:23:32,833
He said anyone could be tempted

498
00:23:32,833 --> 00:23:35,733
by that huge amount of gold
within reach.

499
00:23:35,733 --> 00:23:38,800
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

500
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:40,000
I agree, sir.

501
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:41,100
Prepare a convoy.

502
00:23:42,833 --> 00:23:44,000
You heard him.

503
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:45,600
- Arrange it.
- Yes, sir.

504
00:23:46,567 --> 00:23:47,667
Quimbo.

505
00:23:47,667 --> 00:23:49,333
Sir, yes, sir.

506
00:23:49,333 --> 00:23:51,067
- Put all of it in the bag.
- Okay.

507
00:23:51,067 --> 00:23:52,633
Put the gold bars in the crate.

508
00:23:52,633 --> 00:23:59,533
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

509
00:24:00,733 --> 00:24:01,833
Gabo.

510
00:24:02,600 --> 00:24:05,400
A great deal of money
is at stake here.

511
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:09,467
Bigger than the money
you were earning before.

512
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:14,567
Gabo, remember,

513
00:24:15,500 --> 00:24:17,733
you were in prison
for eight years because of them.

514
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:21,067
You should make
wiser decisions this time.

515
00:24:21,067 --> 00:24:22,900
Oh, Rudy, please!

516
00:24:22,900 --> 00:24:24,800
Don't ruin our conversation.

517
00:24:25,867 --> 00:24:29,900
Why don't you listen
to what they have to say first?

518
00:24:30,700 --> 00:24:33,567
I know Django
and Boss Paquito well.

519
00:24:33,567 --> 00:24:36,933
They don't accept
small time hustles.

520
00:24:40,733 --> 00:24:41,700
Gabo.

521
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:45,000
This is a huge job.

522
00:24:46,100 --> 00:24:47,600
We're talking about gold.

523
00:24:49,933 --> 00:24:51,933
And I know you're the only one
who can pull it off.

524
00:24:52,767 --> 00:24:55,067
I know you got skills
and tricks up your sleeve.

525
00:24:55,933 --> 00:24:57,067
This is easy-peasy for you.

526
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:09,533
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

527
00:25:13,500 --> 00:25:14,833
Gabo doesn't need that.

528
00:25:14,833 --> 00:25:16,900
My son is turning over
a new leaf.

529
00:25:16,900 --> 00:25:18,900
He works an honest job.

530
00:25:18,900 --> 00:25:20,967
He won't accept your offer.

531
00:25:20,967 --> 00:25:24,900
You think so highly
of yourself, Rudy.

532
00:25:24,900 --> 00:25:27,433
The whole Ginintuang Lupa knows

533
00:25:27,433 --> 00:25:30,000
that you badly need the money.

534
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,600
You can barely afford
to buy food.

535
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:36,833
We came here personally
to offer you a job,

536
00:25:36,867 --> 00:25:38,733
and you're telling me
you're going to turn it down?

537
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:42,933
Mister Paquito.

538
00:25:45,967 --> 00:25:47,733
I don't think
I can accept your offer.

539
00:25:48,533 --> 00:25:49,800
I'm a changed man now.

540
00:25:51,600 --> 00:25:53,567
And I don't really trust
your group.

541
00:25:55,767 --> 00:25:56,833
Gabo!

542
00:25:58,000 --> 00:25:59,567
Seriously?

543
00:26:00,800 --> 00:26:03,700
You're refusing this offer?
Are you out of your mind?

544
00:26:03,700 --> 00:26:04,767
Betchay.

545
00:26:05,767 --> 00:26:08,100
If you've sold your soul
to the devil,

546
00:26:09,167 --> 00:26:10,800
that's your choice.

547
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:12,100
Don't drag us down with you.

548
00:26:12,800 --> 00:26:16,100
Well, it looks like we wasted
our time coming here.

549
00:26:16,900 --> 00:26:20,033
We'd better go.

550
00:26:20,033 --> 00:26:23,967
Guys, get the food

551
00:26:23,967 --> 00:26:26,500
and drinks we brought.

552
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:28,633
- Get the barchow.
- Come on!

553
00:26:28,633 --> 00:26:30,500
Bring the barchow.

554
00:26:33,633 --> 00:26:34,600
Gabo.

555
00:26:36,067 --> 00:26:37,500
Who's this woman beside you?

556
00:26:38,867 --> 00:26:39,867
She's beautiful.

557
00:26:40,833 --> 00:26:42,133
Fair skin.

558
00:26:42,167 --> 00:26:44,200
[DJANGO CHUCKLES SLYLY]

559
00:26:44,200 --> 00:26:46,167
This is my first time
seeing her around here.

560
00:26:49,333 --> 00:26:51,067
That's his wife.

561
00:26:51,067 --> 00:26:52,200
Wife?

562
00:26:55,333 --> 00:26:57,067
When did you get married, Gabo?

563
00:27:06,833 --> 00:27:08,567
He got married in prison.

564
00:27:09,167 --> 00:27:10,867
I'm pretty sure

565
00:27:10,867 --> 00:27:13,167
that woman is a criminal too.

566
00:27:13,167 --> 00:27:15,033
She's just acting all sweet.

567
00:27:18,200 --> 00:27:19,767
She's a beautiful
criminal, then.

568
00:27:20,700 --> 00:27:21,933
[DJANGO CHUCKLES]

569
00:27:21,933 --> 00:27:23,067
You don't look good together.

570
00:27:23,067 --> 00:27:26,100
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

571
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:48,567
<i> You chose to have an affair
with someone</i>

572
00:27:48,600 --> 00:27:50,467
<i>who isn't even younger
and prettier than me?!</i>

573
00:27:50,467 --> 00:27:52,267
<i> You're shameless!</i>

574
00:27:52,267 --> 00:27:53,833
<i>We're doing everything
to understand her.</i>

575
00:27:53,833 --> 00:27:55,767
<i> We just endure</i>

576
00:27:55,767 --> 00:27:58,500
<i>and accept all
the hurtful things she says.</i>

577
00:27:58,500 --> 00:27:59,900
<i> The job they're offering
is dangerous!</i>

578
00:27:59,900 --> 00:28:03,600
I won't let Gabo go back to jail
<i> just to earn that much money!</i>

579
00:28:03,600 --> 00:28:05,300
<i> Maybe it's all my fault.</i>

580
00:28:05,300 --> 00:28:06,667
<i> Ever since her baby died,</i>

581
00:28:06,667 --> 00:28:09,133
<i>she has been
treating us all like this.</i>

582
00:28:09,133 --> 00:28:11,833
<i>I feel sorry
for Uncle Rudy and Gabo.</i>

583
00:28:11,833 --> 00:28:14,400
<i> Auntie Betchay is too harsh
on them.</i>

584
00:28:15,733 --> 00:28:18,467
<i>Make sure the gold arrives
at the safe house.</i>

585
00:28:18,467 --> 00:28:21,267
<i>Give me stronger weapons.
And more men.</i>

586
00:28:21,267 --> 00:28:23,433
<i>I can do everything
you ask me to do.</i>

587
00:28:23,467 --> 00:28:24,467
<i> Gabo, we need your help.</i>

588
00:28:24,467 --> 00:28:25,700
<i>Someone broke into
Mister Babot's home.</i>

589
00:28:25,700 --> 00:28:27,433
<i>- Gloria, stay here.
- Where are you going?</i>

590
00:28:27,433 --> 00:28:28,400
<i> Gabo!</i>
